-- allium: 3
-- Spatial paths over clear owned relations.
-- Table events and captured snapshots follow db.allium and allium/live-index.allium.

entity SpatialPath {
    relation: String
    name: String
    generation: Integer
    geometry_column: String
    partition_columns: List<String>
}

entity SpatialPostings {
    path: SpatialPath
    trie: String
    digest: Bytes
}

-- An exact retry preserves the path generation.
-- Dropping a path withdraws its declaration at the ordered system cut and retires the generation's artefacts.
-- A declaration after a drop has a fresh generation.
-- A posting file is a deterministic function of the trie data and the declared geometry and partition columns.
-- The posting file stores partition digests, cells and IIDs as sorted Arrow IPC columns.
-- The builder appends covering keys to typed Arrow columns and sorts their row positions.
-- A held read decodes posting pages against the admitted immutable IPC allocation.
-- A posting read admits the recorded object length and provider scratch before reading its body.
-- Admitted posting and trie provider reads retain the captured catalog until their I/O completes.
-- Each shape contributes the keys of a bounded covering, and each point contributes a leaf with its reported accuracy class.
-- A partition's digest is a candidate key, and the exact read also compares the partition bytes on the resolved row.
-- The exact comparison uses the partition values borrowed from the held read request.
-- A held read uses the path definition, source inventory, and live segments selected by the same snapshot.
-- A prepared filter belongs to its authenticated held read and retains its Arrow partition and parsed region.
-- A continuation sends the filter capability, complete typed identity, bound, and observation flag.
-- Repeating a continuation evaluates the same filter and held cut.
-- Closing a filter or its held read releases the retained filter.
-- A missing or invalid posting file is covered by reading candidate IIDs through the native Arrow page reader within the read budget.
-- The live tail contributes candidate IIDs from its held event batches.
-- One read budget covers all candidate sources and all refined rows.
-- Any candidate set contains every IID whose visible row matches the requested partition and predicate.
-- A complete typed identity contributes at most one result at the chosen valid instant.
-- Complete row history, including delete and erase events, determines visibility before exact geometry refinement.
-- Only visible rows supply geometry to the read's exact predicate.
-- A range page advances in complete typed identity order at the original hold.
-- Nearest ordering compares exact distances and breaks ties by complete typed identity.
-- A document projection includes the resolved document and its system revision in hit order at the original hold.
-- Selection retains the winning row positions until it gathers the final identities and requested document projection.
-- A selected document projection gathers identity, system revision and the requested fields present in the held relation schema.
-- An observed read with an admitted placed witness scope, including an empty page, binds the relation frontier for ordered validation.
-- Erasure orders against the held admission, and its newly compacted source carries no erased posting.
-- Superseded source tries and their derived files follow trie-cat.allium and gc.allium.
